menu "ESPectre Firmware"

config ESPECTRE_TINYUSB_PRIMARY_CONSOLE
    bool "Use TinyUSB CDC as the primary console"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S2
    default n
    help
        Install a TinyUSB CDC ACM device and redirect stdin, stdout, and
        stderr to it. Enable this on ESP32-S2 USB-OTG boards whose ROM USB
        CDC console is not a reliable bidirectional application transport.
        Leave it disabled for UART and USB Serial/JTAG consoles.

config ESPECTRE_EMULATOR_CSI_REPLAY
    bool "Replay recorded CSI inside esp-emu"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3 || IDF_TARGET_ESP32C5 || IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6 || IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
    default n
    help
        Link wrappers for the ESP-IDF CSI calls so CI can replay recorded CSI
        from UART1 when the firmware runs in esp-emu, which models Wi-Fi but
        not CSI. The replay starts only when the factory MAC in eFuse carries
        the emulator marker, which silicon cannot have. On a real chip the
        wrappers pass every call to ESP-IDF and never touch UART1. ESPHome
        and Native link it; esp-emu does not emulate the other targets.

endmenu
